The issue is that the Edit page is using a **Search** endpoint (`SearchCatalogueWeb`) which performs a `Contains` query. When you search for "1", it finds items containing "1" in their ID (like `105805`) or description, instead of the exact item with ID `1`.

You need a dedicated **Get by ID** endpoint.

Here is the fix.

### 1. Add this to `CatalogueEndpoints.cs`

Add this DTO and Endpoint before `return app;`:

```csharp
            // DTO for Get by ID
            public class CatalogueGetRequest
            {
                public long ItemCode { get; set; }
            }

            // 5. Get Catalogue Item Web (By ID)
            app.AddAsyncEndpointWithBearerAuth<CatalogueGetRequest>(
                "GetCatalogueItemWeb",
                async (DataIn, LoginInfo) =>
                {
                    var req = (CatalogueGetRequest)DataIn;
                    using (var ctx = new NewinvContext())
                    {
                        var item = await ctx.Catalogues
                            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => c.Itemcode == req.ItemCode);

                        if (item == null)
                        {
                            throw new ArgumentException($"Catalogue item with code {req.ItemCode} not found.");
                        }
                        return item;
                    }
                },
                "Refresh"
            );
```

