The error `System.Text.Json.JsonException: The JSON value could not be converted to System.Int64` indicates that the deserializer is struggling to convert the string `"2"` to a `long` in your specific `AddAsyncEndpointWithBearerAuth` implementation.

To fix this, we should change the `ItemCode` in the DTO to `string` and parse it manually inside the endpoint. This is safer and avoids the framework's deserialization quirk with primitive types.

Update the DTO and Endpoint in `CatalogueEndpoints.cs`:

```csharp
            // DTO for Get by ID
            public class CatalogueGetRequest
            {
                public string ItemCode { get; set; } // Changed to string to handle deserialization safely
            }

            // 5. Get Catalogue Item Web (By ID)
            app.AddAsyncEndpointWithBearerAuth<CatalogueGetRequest>(
                "GetCatalogueItemWeb",
                async (DataIn, LoginInfo) =>
                {
                    var req = (CatalogueGetRequest)DataIn;

                    // Parse ItemCode manually
                    if (!long.TryParse(req.ItemCode, out long itemCode))
                    {
                        throw new ArgumentException("Invalid ItemCode format.");
                    }

                    using (var ctx = new NewinvContext())
                    {
                        var item = await ctx.Catalogues
                            .FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => c.Itemcode == itemCode);

                        if (item == null)
                        {
                            throw new ArgumentException($"Catalogue item with code {itemCode} not found.");
                        }
                        return item;
                    }
                },
                "Refresh"
            );
