You are absolutely right to be cautious. Using `ExecuteSqlRaw` with string interpolation (`$""`) can be dangerous if not using the specific `ExecuteSqlInterpolated` method. To be completely safe and explicit as per the EF Core manual, we should use `ExecuteSqlRawAsync` with `{0}, {1}` placeholders and pass the values as arguments. EF Core will automatically convert these into database parameters.

Here is the corrected code using explicit parameter placeholders.

```csharp
